Subject: [PATCH] SamsungCamera: create a fallback output file before prepare

The One UI 9 camera can enter the normal recorder path with neither the
filename nor the ParcelFileDescriptor populated on the r9s port.  MediaRecorder
then reaches prepare() without an output writer and returns -11.  Preserve
capture-intent file descriptors, but create the same internal Camera file used
by the normal path when both output forms are absent.

---
 smali_classes4/e9/o.smali | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+)

diff --git a/smali_classes4/e9/o.smali b/smali_classes4/e9/o.smali
--- a/smali_classes4/e9/o.smali
+++ b/smali_classes4/e9/o.smali
@@ -900,6 +900,23 @@
     iget-object v4, p0, Le9/o;->b:Lh7/a;
 
     iget-object v5, v4, Lh7/a;->a:Ljava/lang/Object;
 
+    if-eqz v5, :unica_check_recorder_fd
+
+    goto :unica_recorder_output_ready
+
+    :unica_check_recorder_fd
+    iget-object v6, v4, Lh7/a;->d:Ljava/lang/Object;
+
+    if-eqz v6, :unica_create_recorder_output
+
+    goto :unica_recorder_output_ready
+
+    :unica_create_recorder_output
+    invoke-virtual {p0, v4}, Le9/o;->k(Lh7/a;)V
+
+    iget-object v5, v4, Lh7/a;->a:Ljava/lang/Object;
+
+    :unica_recorder_output_ready
     check-cast v5, Ljava/lang/String;
 
     const-string v7, "RecordingSession"
